WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.912 --> 00:00:05.692
All of us students here at Hillsdale, study
Pericles' Funeral Oration.

00:00:05.692 --> 00:00:11.502
Thucydides records his words to the Athenians,
"The bravest are surely those who have the

00:00:11.502 --> 00:00:16.452
clearest vision of what is before them, glory
and danger alike and yet not withstanding

00:00:16.452 --> 00:00:17.872
go out to meet it."

00:00:17.872 --> 00:00:21.822
A year ago American Conservatives were in
retreat and disarray.

00:00:21.822 --> 00:00:26.882
The media chanted to Republicans, "You must
become moderates or go extinct.

00:00:26.882 --> 00:00:32.702
The spectra of our new president's post Christian,
post American role loomed in progressive dominated

00:00:32.702 --> 00:00:34.412
congress, courts and white house.

00:00:34.412 --> 00:00:38.372
It seemed like there was no line left for
us to hold.

00:00:38.372 --> 00:00:43.902
A few leaders saw the personal and political
dangers of standing fast by principle yet

00:00:43.902 --> 00:00:46.302
forged on with vision.

00:00:46.302 --> 00:00:50.952
As president of the Hillsdale College Republicans,
it's my honor to introduce you to one of those

00:00:50.952 --> 00:00:53.542
leaders, congressman, Mike Pence of Indiana.

00:00:53.542 --> 00:00:57.622
His uncompromising vision was recognized by
The American Conservative Union who honored

00:00:57.622 --> 00:01:01.222
him in 2006 with The Courage Under Fire Award.

00:01:01.222 --> 00:01:06.752
He was named Man of The Year in 2005 by Human
Events, standing among previous recipients

00:01:06.752 --> 00:01:12.432
of this honors such as Justice Clarence Thomas,
Charlton Heston and Ronald Reagan.

00:01:12.432 --> 00:01:16.522
He demonstrated his conviction by standing
against his own party opposing the Prescription

00:01:16.522 --> 00:01:19.082
Drug Benefits Expansion of Healthcare Entitlements.

00:01:19.082 --> 00:01:23.702
He voted against No Child Left Behind because
he believed it undermined local control of

00:01:23.702 --> 00:01:26.292
education through it Federal mandates.

00:01:26.292 --> 00:01:29.552
Something we at Hillsdale ought to know something
about.

00:01:29.552 --> 00:01:33.352
He led the largest caucus in Congress, The
House Republican Study Committee which under

00:01:33.352 --> 00:01:38.662
his chairmanship grew to 110 members and has
consistently given birth to intelligent conservative

00:01:38.662 --> 00:01:41.442
alternatives to the behemoth state.

00:01:41.442 --> 00:01:45.642
Last week on September 12th he told thousands
of Americans standing before the United States

00:01:45.642 --> 00:01:50.222
Capital, "There's nothing that ails this government
that cannot be solved by paying more careful

00:01:50.222 --> 00:01:55.492
attention to the principles enshrined in the
constitution of United States."

00:01:55.492 --> 00:02:00.572
Like the beacon of truth, we shine here at
Hillsdale and now in Washington at the Kirby

00:02:00.572 --> 00:02:05.742
Center, Congressman Pence continues in the
practices of the constitution and in the principles

00:02:05.742 --> 00:02:10.252
of the Declaration of Independence that our
education has instilled in us.

00:02:10.252 --> 00:02:14.812
On behalf of the Hillsdale College Republicans
and Hillsdale College, we are honored to present,

00:02:14.812 --> 00:02:28.132
please welcome the Honorable Congressman,
Mike pence.

00:02:28.132 --> 00:02:55.332
Mike Pence:
President and Mrs. Arnn, Mr. John Cervini.

00:02:55.332 --> 00:03:03.872
Dr. David Bob and Elliot.

00:03:03.872 --> 00:03:09.482
College Republicans and each and every one
of the faculty gathered here today and all

00:03:09.482 --> 00:03:18.651
the students here at Hillsdale College who
have taken time, good evening.

00:03:18.651 --> 00:03:27.151
As I'm sure you know, honor is what allows
us to do what is right despite the cost.

00:03:27.151 --> 00:03:33.071
Even greater honor is required to do what
is right in the face of superior power and

00:03:33.071 --> 00:03:40.842
the greatest honor is to stand strong even
when it means standing alone.

00:03:40.842 --> 00:03:48.882
The long fight at Hillsdale College, standing
alone, then and now for the proposition that

00:03:48.882 --> 00:03:56.712
all men are created equal, then with Fredrick
Douglas, now with Clarence Thomas.

00:03:56.712 --> 00:04:05.802
Then and now in the conviction that Americans
are not horses, we were not born to have saddles

00:04:05.802 --> 00:04:11.172
on our backs, by anyone, at any time, for
any reason.

00:04:11.172 --> 00:04:16.531
This long fight you at Hillsdale have fought.

00:04:16.531 --> 00:04:25.031
For love of ideas that did not come in dreams
or as Reagan said, "Did not spring full bloom

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:29.922
from your brow, but came from the heart of
a great nation."

00:04:29.922 --> 00:04:36.542
Ideas that rose in a time of unprecedented
stress and genius and since the founding have

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:43.562
kept this country whole, prosperous, safe,
just and free.

00:04:43.562 --> 00:04:51.182
It's therefore a profound honor for me to
stand before you in this place, so closely

00:04:51.182 --> 00:04:56.552
associated with the founding of the Republican
Party, in our position to the unforgivable

00:04:56.552 --> 00:05:04.842
sin of slavery, this place where statesmanship
is taught as an art and where right conduct

00:05:04.842 --> 00:05:06.922
is seen its own reward.

00:05:06.922 --> 00:05:19.322
I thank you and may God bless you and God
bless Hillsdale College.

00:05:19.322 --> 00:05:31.922
I rise to pay a debt of honor and a debt to
history.

00:05:31.922 --> 00:05:35.531
My subject today is the presidency.

00:05:35.531 --> 00:05:44.182
My hope is that you will see that institution
in a new light and that you never despair

00:05:44.182 --> 00:05:48.292
of the republic.

00:05:48.292 --> 00:05:52.732
The presidency is the most visible thread
that runs through the tapestry of the American

00:05:52.732 --> 00:05:54.642
government.

00:05:54.642 --> 00:05:57.462
More often than not for good or for ill.

00:05:57.462 --> 00:06:03.872
It sets the tone for the other branches and
spurs the expectations of the people.

00:06:03.872 --> 00:06:08.281
It's powers are vast and consequential.

00:06:08.281 --> 00:06:15.862
It's requirements from the outset and by definition,
impossible for mortals to fulfill without

00:06:15.862 --> 00:06:22.401
humility and insistent attention to its purpose
as set forth in the constitution of the United

00:06:22.401 --> 00:06:25.211
States.

00:06:25.211 --> 00:06:32.042
Isn't it amazing given the great and momentous
nature of the office that those who seek it

00:06:32.042 --> 00:06:37.532
seldom pause to consider what they're seeking?

00:06:37.532 --> 00:06:44.792
Rather unconstrained by principle or reflection,
there seems to be a mad rush towards something

00:06:44.792 --> 00:06:50.292
that once it's powers are seized, the new
president can wield it as an instrument with

00:06:50.292 --> 00:06:58.322
which to transform the nation and the people
according to his highest aspirations.

00:06:58.322 --> 00:07:06.482
Other than in the crisis of a house divided,
the presidency is neither fit nor intended

00:07:06.482 --> 00:07:09.422
to be such an instrument.

00:07:09.422 --> 00:07:18.651
When it is made that, the country sustains
a wound and cries out justly and indignity.

00:07:18.651 --> 00:07:27.362
What the nation says, in the theme of this
address, what it says informed by its long

00:07:27.362 --> 00:07:33.992
history, impelled by the laws of nature and
nature's God, what it says quite naturally

00:07:33.992 --> 00:07:42.102
and rightly if not always gracefully is that
we as a people are not to be ruled and not

00:07:42.102 --> 00:07:45.662
to be commanded.

00:07:45.662 --> 00:07:52.662
It states that the president should never
forget this, that he has not risen above us

00:07:52.662 --> 00:08:02.021
but is merely one of us, chosen by ballot,
dismissed after his term, tasked not to transform

00:08:02.021 --> 00:08:08.352
and work his will upon us but to bare the
weight of decision and to carry out faithfully

00:08:08.352 --> 00:08:17.952
the design laid in the constitution and impassioned
by the Declaration of Independence.

00:08:17.952 --> 00:08:23.302
The presidency must adhere to its definition
as expressed in the constitution and to conduct

00:08:23.302 --> 00:08:29.602
itself, the conduct that is defined over time
and tradition.

00:08:29.602 --> 00:08:34.842
While the powers of the office have in large
with those of the Legislature and the Judiciary,

00:08:34.842 --> 00:08:40.862
the framework of the government was actually
intended to restrict abuses common to classical

00:08:40.862 --> 00:08:45.552
empires and the regal states of the 18th century.

00:08:45.552 --> 00:08:50.482
Without proper adherence to the role contemplated
in the constitution for the presidency, the

00:08:50.482 --> 00:08:56.691
checks and balances of the constitutional
plan become weakened.

00:08:56.691 --> 00:09:01.922
This has been most obvious in recent years
when the three branches of government have

00:09:01.922 --> 00:09:05.821
been subject to the tutelage of a single party.

00:09:05.821 --> 00:09:10.992
Under either party, presidents have often
forgotten that they're intended to restrain

00:09:10.992 --> 00:09:16.862
congress at times and that the congress is
independent of their desires.

00:09:16.862 --> 00:09:25.592
That's fused in some unity, the political
class has raged forward in expansion of powers

00:09:25.592 --> 00:09:33.772
and prerogatives, mistakenly assuming that
to exercise power is by default to do good.

00:09:33.772 --> 00:09:38.871
Even the simplest among us knows that this
is not so.

00:09:38.871 --> 00:09:43.522
Power is an instrument of fatal consequence.

00:09:43.522 --> 00:09:48.672
It is confined no more readily than quick
silver and escapes good intentions as easily

00:09:48.672 --> 00:09:51.681
as air flows through mesh.

00:09:51.681 --> 00:09:57.542
Therefore, those who are entrusted with it
must educate themselves in self-restraint.

00:09:57.542 --> 00:10:14.201
A republic, if you can keep it is about limitation
and for good reason, because we're mortal

00:10:14.201 --> 00:10:18.012
and our actions are imperfect.

00:10:18.012 --> 00:10:26.222
The tragedy of presidential decision is that
even with the best choice, some perhaps many

00:10:26.222 --> 00:10:39.523
will be left behind and some, perhaps many
could die, because of this truth, the true

00:10:39.523 --> 00:10:48.532
statesman lives continuously with what Churchill
called stress of soul, "He may give to Paul

00:10:48.532 --> 00:10:52.722
but only because he robs Peter."

00:10:52.722 --> 00:11:00.891
That is why you must be always weary of a
president who seems to float on his own greatness.

00:11:00.891 --> 00:11:07.081
For all greatness is tempered by mortality,
every soul is equal.

00:11:07.081 --> 00:11:13.462
Distinctions among men cannot be owned, they're
on loan from God who takes them back and evens

00:11:13.462 --> 00:11:17.662
the accounts in the end.

00:11:17.662 --> 00:11:22.292
It's a tragedy indeed the new generations
taking off as attribute failures in governance

00:11:22.292 --> 00:11:28.602
to insufficient power and seek more of it.

00:11:28.602 --> 00:11:33.831
In the Judiciary this is seldom been better
expressed than by Justice Thurgood Marshal

00:11:33.831 --> 00:11:42.071
dictum that, "You do what you think is right
and let the law catch up."

00:11:42.071 --> 00:11:47.581
In the congress it presents itself in massive
legislation, acts and codes, thousands of

00:11:47.581 --> 00:11:54.022
pages long and so monstrously overcomplicated
that no human being can read through them

00:11:54.022 --> 00:12:01.831
in a lifetime, much less understand them,
much less apply them justly to the people

00:12:01.831 --> 00:12:10.362
that increasingly feel that they're no longer
being asked, they're being told.

00:12:10.362 --> 00:12:17.701
Our nation finds itself in the position of
a dog, whose duty is not to ask why because

00:12:17.701 --> 00:12:27.312
the why is too elevated for its nature, it's
simply to obey.

00:12:27.312 --> 00:12:35.941
America is not a dog and does not require
a "Because I said so," jurisprudence to which

00:12:35.941 --> 00:12:42.551
it's then commanded to catch up or legislators
who knit laws of such insulting complexity

00:12:42.551 --> 00:12:52.391
that they're heavier than chains or a president
who acts like, speaks like and is received

00:12:52.391 --> 00:12:55.552
as a king.

00:12:55.552 --> 00:13:08.162
The presidency has run off the rails, it begs
a new clarity, a new discipline, a new president.

00:13:08.162 --> 00:13:17.482
The president is not our teacher, our tutor,
our guide or ruler.

00:13:17.482 --> 00:13:23.472
He does not command us, we command him.

00:13:23.472 --> 00:13:27.821
We serve neither him nor his vision.

00:13:27.821 --> 00:13:37.761
It is not his job or his prerogative to redefine
custom, law and beliefs, to appropriate industries,

00:13:37.761 --> 00:13:45.342
to seize the country as it were by the shoulders
so as to impose by force theatrical charisma

00:13:45.342 --> 00:13:50.011
his justice on 300 million others.

00:13:50.011 --> 00:13:55.632
It is neither his job nor his prerogative
to shift the power of decision away from the

00:13:55.632 --> 00:14:00.862
people to the accolades of his choosing.

00:14:00.862 --> 00:14:05.391
Is my characterization of unprecedented presumptions
incorrect?

00:14:05.391 --> 00:14:14.871
I defer to the judgement of the people which
they will make with their own eyes and ears.

00:14:14.871 --> 00:14:20.492
Listen to the exact words of the leader of
the president's transition team and perhaps

00:14:20.492 --> 00:14:29.212
his next chief of staff, who said two years
age, "It's important that president elect

00:14:29.212 --> 00:14:40.321
Obama is prepared to really take power and
begin to rule day one."

00:14:40.321 --> 00:14:44.662
More recently from the words of the latest
presidential appointment to avoid confirmation

00:14:44.662 --> 00:14:52.352
by the senate, the new head of the Financial
Consumer Bureau wrote last Friday, "President

00:14:52.352 --> 00:14:59.831
Obama understands the importance of leveling
the playing field and creating protections

00:14:59.831 --> 00:15:08.722
that work not just for the wealthy or connected."

00:15:08.722 --> 00:15:14.391
Take power, rule, leveling.

00:15:14.391 --> 00:15:25.641
Though it is now, this has never been and
should never again be the model of the presidency

00:15:25.641 --> 00:15:44.261
or the character of an American president.

00:15:44.261 --> 00:15:52.812
No one can say this too strongly and no one
can say it enough until it is remedied, we

00:15:52.812 --> 00:15:57.472
are not subjects we are citizens.

00:15:57.472 --> 00:16:05.331
We fought our wars so that we don't even have
to treat kings like kings.

00:16:05.331 --> 00:16:12.051
If I may remind you, we won that war.

00:16:12.051 --> 00:16:21.441
Since then the principle of royalty has in
this country been inoperative and who is better

00:16:21.441 --> 00:16:27.672
suited or more required to exemplify this
conviction in word and deed than the president

00:16:27.672 --> 00:16:32.621
of the United states.

00:16:32.621 --> 00:16:39.881
The powers of the presidency are extraordinary
and necessarily great and great presidents

00:16:39.881 --> 00:16:42.352
treat them sparingly.

00:16:42.352 --> 00:16:49.602
For example, it is not the president's job
to manipulate the nation's youth for the sake

00:16:49.602 --> 00:16:52.141
of his agenda or his party's.

00:16:52.141 --> 00:17:01.612
They're a portent political force when amassed
by the social network to which you're incessantly

00:17:01.612 --> 00:17:04.042
connected.

00:17:04.042 --> 00:17:11.522
If the president has their true interest at
heart, he will neither flatter them nor let

00:17:11.522 --> 00:17:14.101
them adore him.

00:17:14.101 --> 00:17:22.992
For in flattery is condensation and in adoration
is direction.

00:17:22.992 --> 00:17:27.882
It's hard to say in this room but youth is
neither seasoned nor tested enough to direct

00:17:27.882 --> 00:17:37.022
a nation, nor should it, the president's business
be to presume to direct them.

00:17:37.022 --> 00:17:41.711
It's difficult enough to do right by your
own kids.

00:17:41.711 --> 00:17:46.682
No one can be the father of all the nation's
youth.

00:17:46.682 --> 00:17:54.481
Is the president therefore expected to turn
away from this and other easy advantage?

00:17:54.481 --> 00:17:56.932
Yes.

00:17:56.932 --> 00:18:03.032
Like Harry Truman who went to bed before the
result on election night, he must know when

00:18:03.032 --> 00:18:16.282
to withdraw, to hold back, to forego attention,
publicity and advantage.

00:18:16.282 --> 00:18:21.362
No finer or more moving or more profound understanding
of the nature of the presidency and the command

00:18:21.362 --> 00:18:30.792
of humility placed upon it has ever been expressed
than by president Coolidge.

00:18:30.792 --> 00:18:35.002
He like Lincoln lost a child while he was
president.

00:18:35.002 --> 00:18:38.822
A son of 16.

00:18:38.822 --> 00:18:44.872
Coolidge wrote, "The day I became president,
my son had just started working in a tobacco

00:18:44.872 --> 00:18:50.972
field when one of his fellow laborer said
to him, if my father was president, I would

00:18:50.972 --> 00:18:59.012
not be working in a tobacco field and young
Mr. Coolidge replied, if my father were you

00:18:59.012 --> 00:19:01.172
father, you would."

00:19:01.172 --> 00:19:11.902
His admiration for the boy was obvious.

00:19:11.902 --> 00:19:18.451
While in the White House president Coolidge's
boy contracted blood poisoning from an incident

00:19:18.451 --> 00:19:24.532
on the south lawn of the White House.

00:19:24.532 --> 00:19:31.652
Coolidge wrote this words that a father can
understand, "What might have happened to him

00:19:31.652 --> 00:19:40.852
under other circumstances we do not know but
if I'd not been president ..." Then he continues

00:19:40.852 --> 00:19:49.382
"In his suffering he was asking me to make
him well and I could not."

00:19:49.382 --> 00:20:03.802
When he went, the power and the glory of the
presidency went with him.

00:20:03.802 --> 00:20:13.512
Sensibility such as this and not power is
the source of presidential dignity and must

00:20:13.512 --> 00:20:16.662
be restored.

00:20:16.662 --> 00:20:24.772
It depends entirely upon character, self-discipline
and an understanding of the fundamental principles

00:20:24.772 --> 00:20:32.992
that underline not only the republic but life
itself.

00:20:32.992 --> 00:20:39.701
It communicates that the president feels the
gravity of his office and is willing to sacrifice

00:20:39.701 --> 00:20:43.262
himself.

00:20:43.262 --> 00:20:50.682
His eye is not upon his own prospects but
on the storm of history through which it is

00:20:50.682 --> 00:21:00.012
his responsibility to navigate with the specific
powers accorded to him and limitations placed

00:21:00.012 --> 00:21:12.462
upon them not merely by man in his desire
but by God in His.

00:21:12.462 --> 00:21:17.981
The modern presidency has drifted far from
the great strength and illumination of its

00:21:17.981 --> 00:21:18.981
source.

00:21:18.981 --> 00:21:26.091
The constitution has given life by the passionate
Declaration of Independence.

00:21:26.091 --> 00:21:34.351
The Constitution terse, sober and specific
does not accept by implication address the

00:21:34.351 --> 00:21:45.111
president's demeanor but this we can read
in the best qualities of the founding generation

00:21:45.111 --> 00:21:50.412
which we would do well to imitate.

00:21:50.412 --> 00:21:58.492
In the Capitol rotunda our heroic paintings,
one of the signing of the Declaration of Independence,

00:21:58.492 --> 00:22:07.402
another of the victory at Saratoga another
of the victory at York Town.

00:22:07.402 --> 00:22:16.062
Something seldom seen in history, there is
a painting of a general, the leader of an

00:22:16.062 --> 00:22:27.122
armed rebellion resigning his commission and
turning his army over to a democratically

00:22:27.122 --> 00:22:31.752
elected government.

00:22:31.752 --> 00:22:36.062
Upon hearing from Benjamin West that George
Washington having won then war and then urged

00:22:36.062 --> 00:22:44.081
to use the army to make himself king would
instead return to his farm, George III said,

00:22:44.081 --> 00:22:51.492
"If he does that, he will be the greatest
man in the world."

00:22:51.492 --> 00:22:58.422
He did and he was.

00:22:58.422 --> 00:23:05.302
To aspire to such virtue and self-restraint
would be in a sense be difficult but in another

00:23:05.302 --> 00:23:09.752
sense, it should be easy.

00:23:09.752 --> 00:23:15.861
Difficult because it would be demanding and
ideal and easy because it is the right thing

00:23:15.861 --> 00:23:25.392
to do and the rewards are immediate and self-evident.

00:23:25.392 --> 00:23:32.152
A president who slights the constitution is
like a rider who hates his horse, he will

00:23:32.152 --> 00:23:51.081
be thrown 

00:23:51.081 --> 00:23:54.512
and the nation along with him.

00:23:54.512 --> 00:24:00.711
The president solemnly swears to preserve,
protect and defend the constitution.

00:24:00.711 --> 00:24:17.032
He does not solemnly swear to ignore, overlook,
supplement or re-interpret it other than in

00:24:17.032 --> 00:24:25.942
a crisis of morality, decency or existence
like the civil war.

00:24:25.942 --> 00:24:30.132
If the president should want to hurry along
the constitution to fit his own notions or

00:24:30.132 --> 00:24:38.032
designs he should do so by amendment rather
than adjustment, for if he joins the powers

00:24:38.032 --> 00:24:46.492
of his office to his own willful interpretation
he steps away from a government of laws and

00:24:46.492 --> 00:24:53.432
toward a government of men.

00:24:53.432 --> 00:24:57.622
Is the constitution a fluctuating and inconstant
document?

00:24:57.622 --> 00:25:04.672
A collection of suggestions, the purpose of
which is to stimulate debate in a future to

00:25:04.672 --> 00:25:10.262
which the founders were necessarily blind?

00:25:10.262 --> 00:25:14.532
Progressives tell us that even the framers
themselves could not reach agreement in its

00:25:14.532 --> 00:25:22.492
regard but they did.

00:25:22.492 --> 00:25:33.702
They did agree upon it and they wrote it down
and they signed it and they lived by it.

00:25:33.702 --> 00:25:41.802
It's words are unchanging and unchangeable
except as planned by careful amendment.

00:25:41.802 --> 00:25:49.632
There's no instruction to the president to
override the law and like Justice Marshal,

00:25:49.632 --> 00:25:52.672
to let it catch up to his superior conception.

00:25:52.672 --> 00:25:58.432
Why is this good?

00:25:58.432 --> 00:26:04.682
It's good because the sun will burn out, the
Ohio river will follow backwards and a cow

00:26:04.682 --> 00:26:10.841
will jump over the moon 10,000 times before
any modern president's conception is superior

00:26:10.841 --> 00:26:30.302
to that of the founders of this nation.

00:26:30.302 --> 00:26:36.842
Would it be such a great surprise that a good
part of the political strife of our times

00:26:36.842 --> 00:26:45.182
is because one president after another rather
than keeping faith to it argues with the document

00:26:45.182 --> 00:26:50.462
he is supposed to live by?

00:26:50.462 --> 00:26:59.812
This discontent will only be calmed by returning
the presidency to the great first principles.

00:26:59.812 --> 00:27:07.711
The president should regard the constitution
and the Declaration like an obsessed lover.

00:27:07.711 --> 00:27:11.872
They should be on his mind all the time.

00:27:11.872 --> 00:27:19.492
The prism through which the light of all questions
of governance passes, that we have sometimes

00:27:19.492 --> 00:27:26.961
gradually, sometimes radically moved away
from this, we can move back to it.

00:27:26.961 --> 00:27:31.861
Who better than the president to restore this
wholesome devotion.

00:27:31.861 --> 00:27:39.981
As the president returns to the consistent
application of the principles of the constitution,

00:27:39.981 --> 00:27:48.492
he will also by doing so ensure fiscal responsibility
and prosperity.

00:27:48.492 --> 00:27:53.711
Who is better suited with his executive and
veto powers to carry over the duty of self-restraint

00:27:53.711 --> 00:27:59.841
to the idea of fiscal solvency than the president
of the United States?

00:27:59.841 --> 00:28:05.591
When the president restraints government spending,
leaving room for the American people to enjoy

00:28:05.591 --> 00:28:12.502
the fruits of their labor, growth is inevitable.

00:28:12.502 --> 00:28:18.361
As Senator Robert Taft wrote, "Liberty has
been the key to our progress in the past and

00:28:18.361 --> 00:28:21.382
is the key to our progress in the future.

00:28:21.382 --> 00:28:27.282
If we can preserve liberty in all its essentials
there is no limit to the future of the American

00:28:27.282 --> 00:28:34.532
people."

00:28:34.532 --> 00:28:52.662
Now, whereas at home the president must be
cautious, dutiful, differential, abroad his

00:28:52.662 --> 00:28:57.392
character must change.

00:28:57.392 --> 00:29:03.902
Were he to ask for a perimeter on how to act
in relation to other states which no holder

00:29:03.902 --> 00:29:09.502
of the office has needed to this point.

00:29:09.502 --> 00:29:16.172
Were that perimeter be written by the American
people in either 1776 or 2010, you can be

00:29:16.172 --> 00:29:23.941
confident it will contain the following instructions.

00:29:23.941 --> 00:29:34.831
You do not bow to kings.

00:29:34.831 --> 00:29:45.721
The president of the United States of America
bows to no man.

00:29:45.721 --> 00:29:59.821
When in foreign lands you do not criticize
your own country.

00:29:59.821 --> 00:30:11.481
You do not argue the case against the United
States but rather the case for it.

00:30:11.481 --> 00:30:25.912
You do not apologize to the enemies of the
United States of America.

00:30:25.912 --> 00:30:40.152
Should you be confused, a country, a people,
a region that harbors, shelters, supports

00:30:40.152 --> 00:30:56.471
or cheers attacks upon our country are enemies
of the United States 

00:30:56.471 --> 00:31:05.752
and to repeat, you do not apologize to them.

00:31:05.752 --> 00:31:15.811
Closely related to this and perhaps the least
ambiguous of the president's complex responsibility

00:31:15.811 --> 00:31:21.692
is his duty as commander in chief of our military.

00:31:21.692 --> 00:31:32.302
In this regard there is a very simple rule,
unknown to some presidents regardless of party.

00:31:32.302 --> 00:31:39.821
If ... It's perhaps the biggest if any president
can face.

00:31:39.821 --> 00:31:48.561
Follow not just him but hundreds of thousands
or millions of others, not just for the rest

00:31:48.561 --> 00:31:57.231
of their lives but in cost of blood and souls
be on life itself.

00:31:57.231 --> 00:32:05.721
If ... It's an if that requires long and deep
hard thought, tremendously hard labor at determining

00:32:05.721 --> 00:32:16.412
the truth of things, a lifetime of education,
a mind of a general, a wisdom of a statesman,

00:32:16.412 --> 00:32:20.802
a heart of infantryman.

00:32:20.802 --> 00:32:31.522
If after careful determination, intense stress
of soul and a deepest prayer, if then you

00:32:31.522 --> 00:33:05.481
go to war and having gone to war by God, you
go to war to win.

00:33:05.481 --> 00:33:11.931
You do not cast away American lives or those
of the innocent non-combatant enemy upon a

00:33:11.931 --> 00:33:16.872
theory of gambit or a notion.

00:33:16.872 --> 00:33:22.002
If the politics of your own election or your
party intrude on your decision for even an

00:33:22.002 --> 00:33:30.282
instant, there're no words for this.

00:33:30.282 --> 00:33:37.312
More common place but hardly less important
are other expectations of the president in

00:33:37.312 --> 00:33:38.312
this regard.

00:33:38.312 --> 00:33:44.302
He must not stint on the equipment and the
provisioning of our armed forces.

00:33:44.302 --> 00:33:51.582
If he airs, it must not be on the side of
scarcity but on the side of surplus.

00:33:51.582 --> 00:33:58.292
He must be the guardian of his troops, taking
every step to avoid even the loss of a single

00:33:58.292 --> 00:34:02.942
American life.

00:34:02.942 --> 00:34:12.252
The American soldier is as precious as the
closest of your kin because he is your kin

00:34:12.252 --> 00:34:18.942
and for his sake the president must in effect
say to the Congress and to the people, "I'm

00:34:18.942 --> 00:34:26.592
commander in chief, it is my sacred duty to
defend the United States and so I demand that

00:34:26.592 --> 00:34:48.142
you give our soldiers everything they need
to complete the mission and come home safe."

00:34:48.142 --> 00:34:56.862
Of all the hardest choices that Congress may
have to make to achieve that end, which one

00:34:56.862 --> 00:35:05.172
of these things alone or in combination is
more terrible than the sacrifice of our children

00:35:05.172 --> 00:35:09.642
or the defeat of our nation?

00:35:09.642 --> 00:35:18.232
If in fulfilling this duty the president waivers
he will have betrayed his office.

00:35:18.232 --> 00:35:30.502
This is not a policy it is probity 
and it is not expedient artifact in my imagination.

00:35:30.502 --> 00:35:45.112
It is written on the blood-soaked ground of
Saratoga, York Town, Antietam, Cold Harbor,

00:35:45.112 --> 00:35:57.353
Guadalcanal, the Pointe du Hoc, the Chosin
Reservoir, Iraq and Afghanistan and a thousand

00:35:57.353 --> 00:36:10.342
other places in our history, in lessons repeated
over and over again.

00:36:10.342 --> 00:36:20.452
The presidency, a great and complex subject
upon which I've only touched has become symbolic

00:36:20.452 --> 00:36:26.002
of overreaching.

00:36:26.002 --> 00:36:31.082
There're many truths that we've been frightened
to tell or face.

00:36:31.082 --> 00:36:39.332
If we run from them, they will catch us with
our backs turned and pull us down, better

00:36:39.332 --> 00:36:49.592
that we should not flee but rather stop and
look them in the eye.

00:36:49.592 --> 00:36:54.732
What might out forbearers say to us knowing
what they knew?

00:36:54.732 --> 00:36:56.702
Having done what they did?

00:36:56.702 --> 00:37:10.042
I have no doubt, they would tell us to channel
our passions, speak the truth and do what's

00:37:10.042 --> 00:37:14.332
right, slowly and with resolution.

00:37:14.332 --> 00:37:22.872
To walk calmly, steadily and without enemies
or fear.

00:37:22.872 --> 00:37:31.472
To be like a rock in the tide, let the water
tumble about us and be firm and unashamed

00:37:31.472 --> 00:37:40.302
in our love of country and so we are.

00:37:40.302 --> 00:37:52.172
I see us like those in Philadelphia in 1776,
danger all around but a fresh chapter, ready

00:37:52.172 --> 00:38:03.622
to begin, uncorrupted, with great possibilities
and inexplicably perhaps miraculously the

00:38:03.622 --> 00:38:07.142
way clearing ahead.

00:38:07.142 --> 00:38:15.782
I have never doubted that providence can appear
in history like the sun emerging from behind

00:38:15.782 --> 00:38:22.902
the clouds if only as a reward for adherence
to first principles.

00:38:22.902 --> 00:38:33.372
As Churchill said, "He must indeed have a
blind soul who cannot see that some great

00:38:33.372 --> 00:38:45.362
purpose and design is being worked out here
below of which we have the honor to be faithful

00:38:45.362 --> 00:38:46.492
servants."

00:38:46.492 --> 00:38:55.712
A long time ago, during the tortured history
of Rome in the 4th century AD, the Emperor

00:38:55.712 --> 00:39:06.922
Constantius, son of the Emperor Constantine
was faced by an ultimatum backed by what appeared

00:39:06.922 --> 00:39:11.822
to be a military force impossible to resist.

00:39:11.822 --> 00:39:21.262
Failure and defeat seemed certain but in the
morning when his answer was due, he said to

00:39:21.262 --> 00:39:33.302
his assembled troops, "Last night, after I
retired to rest a shade of the great Constantine

00:39:33.302 --> 00:39:49.282
rose before my eyes and his well-known voice
forbid me to despair of the republic."

00:39:49.282 --> 00:39:56.272
We too have the voices of shades who emerge
from the past.

00:39:56.272 --> 00:40:02.742
We too have what Lincoln in his first inaugural
called the mystic codes of memory stretching

00:40:02.742 --> 00:40:16.492
from every patriot grave that bind us to the
greats and the humble, the known and the unknown.

00:40:16.492 --> 00:40:30.382
If I hear them clearly, what they say is although
we may have strayed, we have not strayed too

00:40:30.382 --> 00:40:34.302
far to return.

00:40:34.302 --> 00:40:43.592
For we are everyone of us their descendants,
the seniors are still there lively waiting

00:40:43.592 --> 00:40:47.042
to flex.

00:40:47.042 --> 00:40:51.962
We can still astound the world with justice,
reason and strength.

00:40:51.962 --> 00:41:03.992
I know this is true but even if it were not
we could not in decency stand down if only

00:41:03.992 --> 00:41:11.062
for our death to history.

00:41:11.062 --> 00:41:19.042
The death we owe to those who came before,
who did great things, who suffered more that

00:41:19.042 --> 00:41:28.572
we suffer, who gave more than we give and
pledged their lives, their fortunes and their

00:41:28.572 --> 00:41:38.452
sacred honor for us who they did not know
or as the old book says, "We drink from wells

00:41:38.452 --> 00:41:45.232
we did not dig and are warmed by fires we
did not build."

00:41:45.232 --> 00:41:55.112
We must remember and pay our debt to history.

00:41:55.112 --> 00:42:05.002
Many generations are gone but I see them in
my mind's eye and by the character and memory

00:42:05.002 --> 00:42:12.082
of their existence, they forbid us to despair
of the republic.

00:42:12.082 --> 00:42:18.792
I see them crossing the prairies in the sun
and wind and see their faces looking out from

00:42:18.792 --> 00:42:28.522
steel mills and coal mines and immigrant ships
crawling into the harbors at dawn.

00:42:28.522 --> 00:42:35.262
I see them at war, at work and at peace.

00:42:35.262 --> 00:42:44.852
I see them long departed, looking into the
camera with hopeful and sad eyes.

00:42:44.852 --> 00:42:49.372
I see them embracing their children who became
us.

00:42:49.372 --> 00:43:00.292
They are our family and our blood we cannot
desert them, in spirit all of them come down

00:43:00.292 --> 00:43:09.842
to all of us in a connection that out of love,
we cannot betray.

00:43:09.842 --> 00:43:18.212
They're silent now and forever but from the
eternal silence of every patriot grave there's

00:43:18.212 --> 00:43:29.262
yet an echo that says, "It's not too late,
keep faith with us, keep faith with God and

00:43:29.262 --> 00:43:41.492
do not, do not ever despair of the republic."

00:43:41.492 --> 00:43:42.842
Thank you and God bless you.

